---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Worship with us
subtitle: Sabbath service times, where to find us, and what to expect if it's your first visit.
permalink: /worship/
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---

<div class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
    <p class="page-hero__sub">{{ subtitle }}</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="wrap">
  <section class="section section--flush">
    <h2 class="section__title">When we meet</h2>
    <div class="services">
      {% for service in site.services %}
        <div class="service">
          <span class="service__day">{{ service.day }}</span>
          <div class="service__body">
            <h3>{{ service.name }}</h3>
            <p class="service__time">{{ service.time }}</p>
            {% if service.note %}<p class="service__note">{{ service.note }}</p>{% endif %}
          </div>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <p class="note">
      The Sabbath begins at sunset on Friday and ends at sunset on Saturday. Sunset times on
      this island shift a great deal between summer and winter, so our Friday vespers moves
      with them — check the notices or ask us for this week's time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--flush">
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <h2>Where to find us</h2>
        <p class="venue">
          <strong>{{ site.venue_name }}</strong><br />
          {{ site.venue_address }}
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are travelling from outside the city, or you'd like someone to meet you at
          the door, email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> and we will
          arrange it. We would much rather do that than have you wandering around looking for
          the right building.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="callout">
        <h2>Your first Sabbath</h2>
        <p><strong>What should I wear?</strong> Whatever you have. Many of us dress up; nobody is counting.</p>
        <p><strong>What happens?</strong> Sabbath School is Bible study in a small group. Divine Service is the main service — singing, prayer, and a sermon of about forty minutes.</p>
        <p><strong>Will I be put on the spot?</strong> No. Visitors are welcomed warmly, but you will never be made to stand up or speak.</p>
        <p><strong>Are my children welcome?</strong> Very. There are Sabbath School classes for every age group, and no one minds noise.</p>
        <p><strong>Is there food?</strong> Yes. Please stay for it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--flush">
    <div class="callout callout--wide">
      <h2>Prayer requests</h2>
      <p>
        If you would like the church to pray for you — for health, for family, for a
        situation you'd rather not explain in public — email
        <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=Prayer request">{{ site.email }}</a>. Requests
        go only to those who pray over them, and no name is read out without your permission.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
